@baseUrl = http://localhost:5169
@futureDate = 2026-12-01

### Phase 10 walkthrough (REST Client)
### Covers the REST-executable checks from docs/04-phase10-acceptance-checklist.md:
### A2, A3 (REST), B1 (REST), B2 (REST), C1 (REST), D3 (REST)
### Plus validation/contract checks for rows 13/14 from docs/03-execution-plan.md.

### A2) Airports sanity check
# Expected: 200 OK
# Verify: exactly 6 airports and required fields (code, city, country, countryCode)
# Verify specifically: JFK.countryCode == "US" and LHR.countryCode == "GB"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports

### A3) International search (JFK -> LHR)
# @name searchIntl
# Expected: 200 OK
# Verify: isInternational == true
# Verify: flights array has at least 1 item
# Verify per flight: id, provider, flightNumber, origin, destination,
# departureTime, arrivalTime, durationMinutes, cabinClass,
# pricePerPassenger, totalPrice
# Verify: totalPrice = pricePerPassenger * passengers (passengers=1 here)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flights/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "origin": "JFK",
  "destination": "LHR",
  "departureDate": "{{futureDate}}",
  "passengers": 1,
  "cabinClass": "Economy"
}

### A5 REST variant) International booking success (valid passport)
# Expected: 200 OK
# Verify: bookingReference format SR-XXXXXX, status == "Confirmed"
# Verify: totalPrice = pricePerPassenger * passengerCount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "searchId": "{{searchIntl.response.body.$.searchId}}",
  "flightId": "{{searchIntl.response.body.$.flights[0].id}}",
  "passengers": [
    {
      "fullName": "Jane Doe",
      "email": "jane@example.com",
      "documentNumber": "X1234567"
    }
  ]
}

### Row 13 contract check) International booking with invalid document
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
# Verify: validation error for passengers[0].documentNumber
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "searchId": "{{searchIntl.response.body.$.searchId}}",
  "flightId": "{{searchIntl.response.body.$.flights[0].id}}",
  "passengers": [
    {
      "fullName": "Jane Doe",
      "email": "jane@example.com",
      "documentNumber": "123456789"
    }
  ]
}

### B1) Domestic search (JFK -> LAX)
# @name searchDomestic
# Expected: 200 OK
# Verify: isInternational == false
# Verify: flights include providers GlobalAir and BudgetWings
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flights/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "origin": "JFK",
  "destination": "LAX",
  "departureDate": "{{futureDate}}",
  "passengers": 1,
  "cabinClass": "Economy"
}

### B2) Domestic booking success (valid national ID)
# Expected: 200 OK
# Verify: bookingReference format SR-XXXXXX, status == "Confirmed"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "searchId": "{{searchDomestic.response.body.$.searchId}}",
  "flightId": "{{searchDomestic.response.body.$.flights[0].id}}",
  "passengers": [
    {
      "fullName": "John Roe",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "documentNumber": "123456789"
    }
